So, I have been through re-arrangin and moving out some data from R810 '/' t lvm vol '/data', however the restart did not provison all the necessary port connectivity/ bgp distribution the way when I run
'fabric-full.yml' playbook, this indicates, our provisioning is not getting persisted the way it supposed to happen, so any re-start takes it back to the original state.
Due to this reason, we need some hardening and persisting the configuration to the extent it does not load spurious data such as seeing below: We have to persist real configured values to the location 
appropriate for reloading the same data, not the default data such as seeing lots of ip's bgp neighborship in sonic swiches in the log:

